    "turn_text": "First of all, it's not a boring job. I granted that. I really think the Democrats are doing themselves a real disservice. All the disruptions, I mean, they just come across as rude and not with particularly good arguments. If this is just about a process that they didn't get enough paper, you know, I think the Republicans have done a pretty good job of repeating that. The almost half a million pages is more pages of information than was turned over in the last five nominees. And let's face it, the Democrats have more than enough information to make an evaluation of what kind of judge Kavanaugh has been, what kind of justice he will be, what kind of human being is. And so they have more than enough information. There's so many of them, including our own Senator Baldwin, already declared they would know before they probably even looked at one piece of",
