    "turn_text": "Ted Kennedy is responsible for creating a whole new word a verb called borking uh... when he borked robert bork uh... that's really what change i mean prior to that you had school year you had gensberg to completely different uh... judges ideologically yet they were confirmed overwhelmingly that both of them got more than any votes and again that that's because prior to ted kennedy borking robert bork uh... there was a assumption that elections matter that presence got to nominate people who agreed with their philosophy and and you had a senate that you basically say that that makes sense to us but democrats return this into an i i i i i i i'd let us test they want super legislators they've also found out over the years that their liberal policies their their brand of socialism doesn't sell very well they can't pass it to legislators so the only way they can get their policy preference over regulation uh... those types things is to judiciary so that they they'd literally live off of super legislators activist juris and that's all they want really appointed on uh... on courts throughout the land it's been the singular achievement really one of the singular achievements of uh... present trumps administration together with republican senate we have confirmed twenty-six circuit court nominees uh... now hopefully two supreme court nominees a a a bunch of the district courts and and we're just populating with judges Which by the way, it's big difference. We're still disadvantaged. We're confirming judges. They will apply the law. A lot of law we disagree with. Okay. There are plenty of decisions of Brett Kavanaugh. I wasn't particularly happy with, but he filed the law. He applied it. He probably wasn't real happy with the result. But again, his job as a judge is to interpret and apply the law, not alter it. Democrats want judges that will alter the law. They will make policy. They'll make law. And so we're still disadvantaged, but that's why it's so important. Elections matter. If you are concerned about the Constitution, if you believe laws should be applied, not altered, it's very important that we maintain a majority here in the Senate, in the House, and we continue to elect presidents like Trump who will appoint judges, not super legislators.",
