  {
    "episode_id": 90834,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90834.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Well, I actually spoke to Senator Feinstein in the morning. And again, I think you'd probably like to see hearing go slightly different direction in terms of just civility. But what I've been able to watch and what I've heard In terms of his response to questions, they've just been outstanding. He's showing himself to be unbelievably highly qualified, which again just makes it that much more difficult. I did listen to Ted Cruz's opening statement. He talked about, you know, in law, when the facts on your side, you pound the facts. When the laws on your side, you pound the law. When you got needed of those two, you just pound the table. And that's really what the Democrats are reverting to. They're primal scream. They're just pounding the table. and distracting from really the extraordinary background and really the excellent responses he's given to their questions.",
