    "turn_text": "individual liberty, obviously you have to provide a secure and safe environment. You need to defend our nation. You have to secure our borders. And in terms of defense of the nation, we do a pretty good job. We've been working overtime. We have not been hit. We haven't had an airplane attack since 9-11, since we hardened our cockpits. Again, a very simple solution, but very effective. When it comes to securing our borders, that has been a problem that has vexed multiple administrations and nobody hit until this administration has really dedicated their administration and really spent the political capital to attempt to do it. From my standpoint, the first thing we have to do is we have to change our laws that incentivize the illegal immigration. One of them is the floor's decision, the reinterpretation, which really forces ICE and CBP to either catch and release individuals or separate parents from their children. And that's what has played out here. But again, what we have done because of the new policy, we're not going to separate kids anymore. Nobody likes to see that. We really are back to full catch and release. And because CBP and ICE really can't determine in 20 days, Is that really the father? Or is that a sex trafficker?",
